Third-party data
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Coldframe's code is MIT licensed. The scientific data it processes is not, and
carries its own terms. Redistribution terms per source are recorded in
data-sources.json, which the build script reads to decide what may be published.

Artifacts built by scripts/build-locus.mjs contain material derived from:

1. AraCLIM (Arabidopsis CLIMtools)
   https://github.com/CLIMtools/AraCLIM
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
   http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

   Coldframe uses the geo-climate variable table and accession roster. Values
   are subset and reformatted; they are not otherwise modified. This portion
   remains under Apache-2.0 and is not relicensed as MIT.

   Cite: Ferrero-Serrano, A. & Assmann, S.M. (2019). Phenotypic and genome-wide
   association with the local environment of Arabidopsis. Nature Communications.

2. 1001 Transcriptomes (NCBI GEO accession GSE80744)
   https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSE80744
   US Government work; public domain.

   Cite: Kawakatsu, T. et al. (2016). Epigenomic Diversity in a Global
   Collection of Arabidopsis thaliana Accessions. Cell 166:492-505.

3. Ensembl Plants, Arabidopsis thaliana TAIR10 annotation
   https://plants.ensembl.org/
   No restrictions on use or redistribution.

4. arabidopsis.png - photograph of Arabidopsis thaliana in flower
   (c) Marie-Lan Nguyen / Wikimedia Commons
   Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 2.5 Generic (CC BY 2.5).
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.5
   https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arabidopsis_thaliana_JdP_2013-04-28.jpg

   Cropped and scaled for use in the page footer; not otherwise modified.
   The credit also appears in the footer note beside the photograph, since
   CC BY requires attribution to travel with the work.

5. Natural Earth 110m land polygons (src/coastline.json)
   https://www.naturalearthdata.com/
   Public domain.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Not redistributed
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1001 Genomes v3.1 genotype calls
   https://1001genomes.org/
   Cite: 1001 Genomes Consortium (2016). Cell 166:481-491.

   No explicit redistribution grant exists for this callset, so per-accession
   genotype calls are excluded from published Coldframe artifacts. Artifacts
   built with --public carry per-site allele frequencies and environmental
   correlations derived from the calls, which are facts about the data rather
   than a subset of it. To obtain the calls themselves, run scripts/fetch-raw.sh,
   which retrieves them from the 1001 Genomes VCFSubset API directly.
